# Drafted by Gemini (R14 gareth), edited.

~ after
Narrator: The room above the taproom smells of boiled wool and old tallow, and Gareth sits with his back braced hard against the chimney bricks.
gareth_creed [weary]: I still hear those bells in my teeth, friends, and I cannot quite get my hands to stop shaking. Still, a cold room in Dawn's Gate beats a dry stack of kindling up on that mountain.
* We are glad to see you breathing, Gareth. -> g_thanks
* Tell us what you found up at the monastery. -> g_saw
* Melina is waiting in Wickermoor. You should go home. -> g_home
* Rest while you can. We will leave you be. -> END

~ g_thanks
gareth_creed [smile]: It is me who owes you my hide, and every breath left in it. They had me measured for the third night's fire before you came through that door.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Get your boots dry, lad, and sign the log when you're steady.
-> after

~ g_saw
gareth_creed [afraid]: A young stable hand slipped me an old prior's journal before the hounds caught my scent. That Crimson Rose they pray to is no goddess at all, just a laughing devil wearing Father Renathyr like a glove.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Wearing the Abbot like a glove? Your Foolishness says he hates a copycat puppeteer.
-> after

~ g_home
gareth_creed [neutral]: Give me until the Sanguine Hunt rides back up the ridge and the river road clears. The moment the snow settles, I will walk straight back to Wickermoor and tell Melina and Preacher Murdoch everything.
set gareth_home
-> END
